## Why This License Structure

A framework that teaches resistance to Control cannot control access to its own principles. A framework whose Reciprocity Principle asks of AI nothing it does not also ask of the institutions building AI cannot itself withhold what it asks others to share. These licenses reflect the Standard's own stance: open availability, free adoption, and no gatekeeping.

The Meridian AI Standard is explicitly designed for adoption by AI organizations, alignment teams, internal risk teams, external auditors, and anyone running open-weights models who wants to apply the Standard themselves. Any organization or individual may adopt, adapt, and build upon it. The CC BY 4.0 license ensures this remains legally unambiguous.

Attribution keeps adapted versions connected to their source. The Standard is a living document: it is revised, versioned and corrected over time. We ask those who adapt it to make the original easy to find, so that anyone who meets an adapted version — an organization's implementation, a translation, a derivative framework, a quoted excerpt — can trace it back to [meridianstandard.ai](https://meridianstandard.ai) and compare the two. The license itself requires credit and a link to the license; the link back to the original is our request.
